Closures, explicit currying, shadowing, recursion, and zero-argument functions.
$[Import* std]
${{{^ {a} {^ {b} {- a b}}} 10} 3}
expect: 7
$[# {adder n} {^ {x} {+ x n}}]
$[# add5 {adder 5}]
${add5 1} ${map {' 1 2} {adder 10}} ${{compose {adder 1} {adder 2}} 0}
expect: 6
expect: [11, 12]
expect: 3
$[# even {^ self {n} {!if {= n 0} true {!if {= n 1} false {self {- n 2}}}}}]
${even 10} ${even 7}
expect: true
expect: false
${{^ {map} map} 4}
expect: 4
${{^ {x} {{^ {x} {* x 10}} {+ x 1}}} 1}
expect: 20
$[# {k} 42]
${k} ${{const k 0}} ${{^ {} {{^ {} 1}}}}
expect: 42
expect: 42
expect: 1
$[# {fib n} {!if {< n 2} n {+ {fib {- n 1}} {fib {- n 2}}}}]
${fib 20}
expect: 6765
$[# count {^ loop {n acc} {!if {= n 0} acc {loop {- n 1} {+ acc 1}}}}]
${count 20000 0}
expect: 20000
A recursive lambda's name is local to it; inner closures may capture it, and it can be returned.
$[# countTo {^ next {n limit} {^ {} {!if {>= n limit} n {{next {+ n 1} limit}}}}}]
${{countTo 1 4}}
expect: 4
